<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore Roosevelt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore Roosevelt was the 26th president of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, from 1901 to 1909. A hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-american-war">Spanish–American War</a>, he pursued an assertive 'big stick' policy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>, backing Panama's secession from Colombia in 1903 to build the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a> and claiming a right to intervene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America</a> under the Roosevelt Corollary. He won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a> for mediating the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a> in 1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt.jpg" alt="Theodore Roosevelt" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adam Cuerden · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theodore_Roosevelt_by_the_Pach_Bros_(4x5_cropped)_(3).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Liberation Army general Pino Guerra raised the revolt, Estrada Palma arrested every Liberal politician within reach, and when <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b>'s emissaries sought a compromise rather than back him he resigned with his whole cabinet, forcing the United States to take control until 1909, when José Miguel Gómez was…</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-cuba-1902-1959">Republic of Cuba (1902-1959) · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Panama’s independence, won under the protection of American warships, became a classic example of ‘big stick’ diplomacy, and <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b> later boasted that he had taken the isthmus.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Republic of Panama · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1912 <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b> declared that the initiative and referendum should be used “not to destroy representative government, but to correct it whenever it becomes misrepresentative”.</blockquote><a href="/government/direct-democracy">Direct democracy · Through History</a></li><li><blockquote>In the United States <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b> held that wise progressivism and wise conservatism go hand in hand, and the word conservative was first used in its modern sense for pro-free enterprise opponents of the New Deal; the Republican Party became the country’s major conservative party.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/conservatism">Conservatism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>With <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b> and William Howard Taft splitting the Republican vote, the Democrat Woodrow Wilson won the presidency.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-5">5 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Republican President William McKinley defeated the Democrat William Jennings Bryan in a rematch of the 1896 election, with Governor <b>Theodore Roosevelt</b> of New York as his running mate.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-6">6 November in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. Died in Sagamore Hill, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.73,-73.99&amp;year=1897" aria-label="Manhattan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2737 709 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Theodore Roosevelt"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3187 979h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3187 979h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.73,-73.99&amp;year=1897">What was here in 1897? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
